<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great King</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Great King was a royal title used in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">ancient Near East</a> for rulers of major powers who recognised each other as equals. The Hittite Great King at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> held military, judicial and religious authority, and unlike Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-kingship">divine kingship</a> he was viewed as the earthly representative of the gods.</p></div>
